wikipedia_extract: Aquila (Italian for "Eagle") was an Italian aircraft carrier converted
  from the transatlantic passenger liner SS Roma. During World War II, work on Aquila
  began in late 1941 at the Ansaldo shipyard in Genoa and continued for the next two
  years. With the signing of the Italian armistice on 8 September 1943, however, all
  work was halted and the vessel remained unfinished. She was captured by the National
  Republican Navy of the Italian Social Republic and the German occupation forces
  in 1943, but in 1945 she was partially sunk by a commando attack of Mariassalto,
  an Italian royalist assault unit of the Co-Belligerent Navy of the Kingdom of Italy,
  made up by members of the former Decima Flottiglia MAS. Aquila was refloated and
  scrapped in 1952.
